% ============================================================================
% mineral-hardness.query.adj — a worked recall over the geology
% mineral-hardness library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "how hard is quartz on the
% Mohs scale?": it states no geology fact — it only `import`s the grounded table
% and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `mineral_hardness` rows and returns the number + the table's source/locator/
% trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the value 10, recall
% the mineral that has it — diamond). Graphite is not one of the ten reference
% minerals of the scale, so a recall on it abstains honestly — the engine never
% invents a hardness.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli mineral-hardness.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "mineral-hardness.adj"

? mineral_hardness(talc, $H)      % expect 1  — softest
? mineral_hardness(quartz, $H)    % expect 7  — middle of the scale
? mineral_hardness(corundum, $H)  % expect 9
? mineral_hardness($M, 10)        % expect diamond — reverse recall
? mineral_hardness(graphite, $H)  % expect abstain — not a Mohs reference mineral
